  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "After Hu Immortal blessed land gains blood path dao marks from the blood poison kerria earthly calamity, exquisite flower buds mature into red axe flowers. The petals are like axe blades, white but giving off a hint of red light. Together with blood sickle grass, they are excellent Gu refinement materials. They are not immortal materials, but they can be used to refine rank three mortal Gu. Mature seas of the flowers across the blessed land can become a large source of wealth.",
      "chapters": [
        826
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance-and-use",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_immortal_blessed_land",
        "sys_mortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Poisonous blood in the soil converts part of earlier flowers’ and grasses’ roots and seeds into seeds of blood sickle grass and red axe flowers, and the new blood path dao marks create the environment they need to grow. Fang Yuan digs poisonous blood lakes so seepage under Gu formations constantly nourishes both plants.",
      "chapters": [
        826
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance-and-use",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_gu_formation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A sparse grassland of wildflowers and grass is mainly blood sickle grass and red axe flowers.",
      "chapters": [
        1291
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sparse-grassland",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In Mini Northern Plains, Fang Yuan works to create a blood red grassland with blood sickle grass and red axe flowers as the foundation for pink flower rabbits, wolves, and foxes.",
      "chapters": [
        1461
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "blood-red-grassland",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_mini_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Red axe flowers appear in a list of flower Gu materials alongside ghost face sunflowers, wire cotton, heavenly flowers, seven treasure flowers, milk tea flowers, and others.",
      "chapters": [
        1479
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
